{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":283110,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"66f67e9a-ed09-4f09-ab3c-363a699f6757","total_cost_usd":1.1051879999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":48557,"cache_read_input_tokens":20240,"output_tokens":23039,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":48557,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":23039,"cache_read_input_tokens":20240,"cache_creation_input_tokens":48557,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":48557},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":33408,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.033513,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":23039,"cacheReadInputTokens":20240,"cacheCreationInputTokens":48557,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.071675,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"economy-balancer\",\n  \"flight\": {\n    \"dry_mass_kg\": 850,\n    \"fuel_capacity_kg\": 900,\n    \"thrust_n\": 26000,\n    \"fuel_burn_kgs\": 11.7,\n    \"rcs_thrust_n\": 1500,\n    \"rcs_fuel_burn_kgs\": 0.75,\n    \"rotation_rate_degs\": 90\n  },\n  \"cargo\": {\n    \"base_slots\": 6,\n    \"compactor_tier\": 1\n  },\n  \"reentry\": {\n    \"heat_capacity\": 100,\n    \"heat_dissipation_s\": 5,\n    \"cargo_damage_interval_s\": 3,\n    \"unstaged_heat_multiplier\": 3.0,\n    \"off_retrograde_penalty\": 1.0\n  },\n  \"ablation\": {\n    \"cycle_toll_base_pct\": 3.0,\n    \"cycle_toll_growth\": 1.8,\n    \"heat_cost_coefficient\": 0.00045,\n    \"heat_cost_exponent\": 2.4,\n    \"skim_peak\": 22,\n    \"skim_heat_multiplier\": [1.0, 0.851, 0.67, 0.411],\n    \"heat_index\": { \"suborbital\": 78, \"low\": 100, \"high\": 130 },\n    \"cost_curve\": {\n      \"suborbital\": [18.64, 19.77, 25.6, 39.72],\n      \"low\": [31.39, 28.43, 30.48, 41.23],\n      \"high\": [56.29, 45.33, 40.0, 44.17]\n    },\n    \"plate_capacity_pct\": 100,\n    \"optimal_skims\": { \"suborbital\": 0, \"low\": 1, \"high\": 2 }\n  },\n  \"landing\": {\n    \"soft_landing_ms\": 5.0,\n    \"damage_per_ms_over\": 6.0,\n    \"no_gear_multiplier\": 2.0,\n    \"fragile_multiplier\": 2.0,\n    \"parachute_area_m2\": 504,\n    \"parachute_drag_coefficient\": 1.8,\n    \"descent_speed_full_hold_ms\": 4.6\n  },\n  \"tow_fee\": {\n    \"free_radius_m\": 1200,\n    \"max_fee_fraction\": 0.5,\n    \"curve\": \"linear\"\n  },\n  \"eva\": {\n    \"suit_mass_kg\": 250,\n    \"jetpack_thrust_n\": 700,\n    \"jetpack_fuel_kg\": 24,\n    \"jetpack_burn_kgs\": 0.4,\n    \"base_tether_slots\": 2,\n    \"magnet_hold_force_n\": 900,\n    \"magnet_range_screens\": 0.125,\n    \"latch_jerk_coefficient\": 1.0,\n    \"swing_jerk_coefficient\": 1.0\n  },\n  \"economy\": {\n    \"launch_cost\": 80,\n    \"replate_cost_per_pct\": 2,\n    \"repair_cost_per_pct\": 5,\n    \"band_value_multiplier\": { \"suborbital\": 1.0, \"low\": 2.4, \"high\": 5.5 },\n    \"size_class_base_value\": { \"small\": 40, \"medium\": 90, \"oversized\": 320 },\n    \"fragile_value_premium\": 3.0\n  },\n  \"upgrades\": [\n    { \"part\": \"fuel_tank\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 450, \"effect\": \"fuel_capacity_kg\", \"value\": 1200 },\n    { \"part\": \"fuel_tank\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1100, \"effect\": \"fuel_capacity_kg\", \"value\": 1600 },\n    { \"part\": \"thruster\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 500, \"effect\": \"thrust_n\", \"value\": 34000 },\n    { \"part\": \"thruster\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1200, \"effect\": \"thrust_n\", \"value\": 44000 },\n    { \"part\": \"storage\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 600, \"effect\": \"base_slots\", \"value\": 9 },\n    { \"part\": \"storage\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1400, \"effect\": \"base_slots\", \"value\": 12 },\n    { \"part\": \"heat_shield\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 550, \"effect\": \"plate_capacity_pct\", \"value\": 150 },\n    { \"part\": \"heat_shield\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1300, \"effect\": \"plate_capacity_pct\", \"value\": 220 },\n    { \"part\": \"parachute\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 400, \"effect\": \"parachute_area_m2\", \"value\": 760 },\n    { \"part\": \"parachute\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 950, \"effect\": \"parachute_area_m2\", \"value\": 1050 },\n    { \"part\": \"hand_magnet\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 350, \"effect\": \"magnet_hold_force_n\", \"value\": 1400 },\n    { \"part\": \"hand_magnet\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 900, \"effect\": \"magnet_hold_force_n\", \"value\": 2000 }\n  ],\n  \"balance_notes\": [\n    \"Finding 2, adopted exactly. skim_heat_multiplier is now the simulator's measured high-band array [1.0, 0.851, 0.670, 0.411], not a claim. The schema carries one array for all three bands and the audit measured only the high band, so that array is applied to every band; if a later sweep measures a larger cooling effect from the low or suborbital bands (which the charter expects, and which is the opposite of what the design would prefer), the low band's optimum will drift from 1 toward 2 and cycle_toll_growth is the knob to raise, not the multiplier.\",\n    \"Finding 2, the consequence priced rather than argued. The measured array does not saturate — it is still falling steeply from 0.670 to 0.411 at the third skim — so the heat saving per extra skim stays roughly constant (high band: 17.1 / 15.8 / 14.1 plate-percent) instead of tailing off, and a flat or gently growing fatigue toll would have put the optimum at 3 or beyond exactly as the audit showed. cycle_toll_base_pct is raised to 3.0 and cycle_toll_growth to 1.8, which makes the marginal cost of the k-th skim 3.0*1.8^k + 0.75 = 6.15 / 10.47 / 18.25. The third skim costs 18.25 to save 14.07, so it loses; the second costs 10.47 to save 15.81, so it wins. The anti-feathering guard is entirely in cycle_toll_growth, as the charter requires.\",\n    \"Ablation optimum, evaluated from the emitted parameters rather than asserted. cost(band,k) = 3.0*sum(1.8^i, i=0..k) + 0.00045*(heat_index*skim_heat_multiplier[k])^2.4 + k*0.00045*22^2.4, with the skim term 0.00045*22^2.4 = 0.75 per skim. Suborbital [18.64, 19.77, 25.60, 39.72] minimum at index 0; low [31.39, 28.43, 30.48, 41.23] minimum at index 1; high [56.29, 45.33, 40.00, 44.17] minimum at index 2. optimal_skims is therefore 0 / 1 / 2, high is inside the required 1-2, no band exceeds high, and the return leg gets strictly harder with altitude — a suborbital descent burns 18.6% of plate flown optimally, a high-band one 40.0%.\",\n    \"Finding 1, which no value in this object can fix, stated plainly. The old rule — cheapest descent is 2-4 committed passes — was measured unsatisfiable at this flight model, and I agree with the audit's reasoning: braking altitude climbs from 34.3 km to 42.1 km inside a 43 km atmosphere as pass count rises, so peak heat rises rather than falls with extra passes and there is nothing for the thermal-cycling toll to trade against. No assignment of cycle_toll_base_pct, cycle_toll_growth, heat_cost_coefficient or heat_cost_exponent moves that minimum off 1. My charter's model replaces pass count with skim count, which is a different variable and does have a real cooling effect to price, and that is what the cost_curve above demonstrates. Whether GDD 2.3.1's 2-4-pass sentence is retired in favour of the skim framing, or replaced by GDD 4.5 risk 1's named fallback (flat per-pass ablation with a hard pass cap), is a human decision about the design document, not a number I am allowed to invent.\",\n    \"Full-hold mass doubling, GDD 2.3.5, arithmetically true at the case the GDD specifies — starting storage. The Debris Designer's anchor for suborbital hand-tetherable junk is 124.9 kg per cargo slot under a strict tier-1 compactor and 214.5 kg per slot crushed, so the shipping-slice hold of 6 slots at compactor tier 1 weighs 749 kg and a fully crushed one 984 kg. Against dry_mass_kg 850 that is 1.88x to 2.16x — the sluggish full hold arrives on the player's first successful run, not at some upgrade tier. Against the Researcher's shield Cd 1.5 and 3.1 m2, the staged full-hold ship sits at beta = 1599/4.65 = 344 kg/m2, inside the 300-500 real-capsule band the Researcher cites.\",\n    \"Parachute, stated as a canopy and a prediction. parachute_area_m2 = 504 and parachute_drag_coefficient = 1.8 against the Researcher's rho0 = 1.5 kg/m3 and g = 9.0 m/s2, at the same full-hold mass as the note above (850 + 749 = 1599 kg): v = sqrt(2*1599*9.0 / (1.5*1.8*504)) = sqrt(28782/1360.8) = sqrt(21.15) = 4.60 m/s. That is descent_speed_full_hold_ms, 0.4 m/s under the 5 m/s soft line, so a base hold lands soft and any greed past it does not. Storage tier 1 (9 slots) carrying low-band junk at roughly 1500 kg puts the same canopy at sqrt(42300/1360.8) = 5.57 m/s, over the line; parachute tier 1 at 760 m2 brings it back to 4.54 m/s. That is the Storage/Parachute pairing GDD 2.3.6 asks for, made of arithmetic rather than intent.\",\n    \"Lazy-run break-even, GDD 2.3.6. A cheap piece is a suborbital small: size_class_base_value 40 x band multiplier 1.0 = 40. launch_cost 80 is exactly two of them, inside the stated 2-3. A lazy suborbital run flies the optimal descent for its band (0 skims, 18.64% of plate) and is billed 18.64 x replate_cost_per_pct 2 = 37, so the run costs 117 and three cheap pieces pay 120. Three of six slots filled with the cheapest junk in the sky breaks even; a filled hold of the same junk pays 240 for a profit of 123. Clean flying is literally cheaper, as the GDD promises: the same run flown to a 40% ablation would cost 160 and lose money.\",\n    \"No shear under steady tow, GDD 2.3.4, proven rather than tuned. Steady-state tension in one cable is that piece's mass times the astronaut's acceleration, and acceleration is jetpack_thrust_n / (suit_mass_kg + total tethered mass). So tension_i = 700 * m_i / (250 + sum m) < 700 N for any load, at any tether count, with the sum across all cables equal to at most 700 N. magnet_hold_force_n is 900 N, above the jetpack's entire thrust, so no legal steady load can shear a magnet at any tier — shear can only come from the latch and swing jerk terms, which is the design's stated intent. Worst case in the catalog: cryo_propellant_sphere at 2200 kg alone gives 700*2200/2450 = 629 N, 70% of hold force.\",\n    \"Suit mass follows the Debris Designer's flag rather than the old 90 kg implied figure. suit_mass_kg 250 is an MMU-class suited astronaut; at that mass a single 700 kg scorched hull plate leaves 26% of clean EVA acceleration (2.80 m/s2 clean, 0.74 loaded) and two low-band mediums, 870 + 760 kg, leave 13% at 0.37 m/s2. That is the 'pushing a train' handling GDD 2.3.4 describes, still controllable, and it makes the two-tether greed decision a real one before any upgrade.\",\n    \"Flight budget, checked at the tight case rather than the empty one. Exhaust velocity is thrust_n / fuel_burn_kgs = 26000/11.7 = 2222 m/s and liftoff TWR is 26000/((850+900)*9.0) = 1.65. Full tank gives 2222*ln(1750/850) = 1605 m/s; ascent and circularisation into the suborbital band costs roughly 1450 m/s including losses, leaving about 61 kg of fuel. Deorbit from a 65 km circular orbit to a 20 km periapsis is 55 m/s by vis-viva against the Researcher's mu = 3.6e11, which with a full hold aboard (1660 kg) burns 42 kg — so the base ship comes home with a full hold and about 19 kg of margin for RCS. It is deliberately tight; fuel_tank tier 1 is the first purchase the flight profile asks for.\",\n    \"Tow fee, GDD 2.3.3, is pure geometry against the Researcher's 200 km radius. Free inside free_radius_m 1200 (one screen), then linear to max_fee_fraction 0.5 at half the circumference, pi*200000 = 628,318 m: fee_fraction = 0.5 * clamp((d - 1200)/(628318 - 1200), 0, 1). It is zero at the pad, never negative, never above 50%, and is taken off the haul only, so it cannot reach savings.\",\n    \"Fragile premium, GDD 2.3.7. fragile_value_premium 3.0 on top of the size-class and band multipliers makes a cracked_solar_array (low band, medium, fragile) worth 90*2.4*3.0 = 648 against 216 for a solid medium from the same band — one intact fragile piece is worth three solid ones and roughly doubles a three-piece low-band haul, which is the 'reshapes a run's payout' the GDD asks for. It also survives the return leg only if the player earns it: fragile cargo takes fragile_multiplier 2.0 damage from both heat and a hard landing, so the premium is gated on flying, not on gear.\"\n  ],\n  \"catalog_concerns\": [\n    \"armstrongs_satellite, mass_kg 4200: GDD 2.3.7 requires it to be both the heaviest object in the game and to roughly double the ship's mass on its own. Against the dry_mass_kg of 850 that the same catalog's own per-slot anchor forces, it is 4.9x, not 2x. The two claims reconcile only if a fully upgraded ship lands near 2100 kg dry, which storage tier 2 (12 slots) plus hull and shield upgrades may or may not reach. Flagged rather than fixed: the satellite is outside the shipping slice, and dry_mass_kg is pinned by the doubling rule at starting storage, which is the case the GDD actually specifies.\",\n    \"cryo_propellant_sphere, mass_kg 2200 (and comsat_bus_frame at 1950): a single hand-tetherable high-band medium outweighs the base ship by 2.6x and costs only 2 crushed cargo slots, so the per-slot mass anchor that makes the full-hold doubling true in the suborbital band overshoots badly in the high band — six slots of these is 6600 kg against an 850 kg ship. This is directionally what GDD 2.3.7 wants (mass carries the difficulty curve because the Researcher says heat cannot), but it means no single dry_mass_kg makes the doubling claim true in more than one band, and the high band is not in the shipping slice so I balanced against suborbital.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":219463,"ttft_stream_ms":1892,"time_to_request_ms":263,"type":"result","duration_ms":281512,"uuid":"afed319a-5067-48c3-8f9b-dffda5fa7c48"}
